    "title": "New charge in Aimee Cotton case - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By The Martha's Vineyard Times ,\n5 hours ago Aimee Cotton of Oak Bluffs, who pleaded not guilty in October 2025 after being indicted by a Dukes County grand jury of manslaughter and reckless endangerment of a child in September, was indicted for murder today in the Dukes County Superior Court, according to court documents. Courtney L. Scalice was added as the prosecutor for the Cape and Islands District Attorney’s office, also according to court documents. Read full article",
